{"name":"Happy Margarine","hex":"#e0dabf","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"happy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a feeling arising from a consciousness of well-being or of enjoyment; enjoying good of any kind, such as comfort, peace, or tranquillity; blissful, contented, joyous.","Experiencing the effect of favourable fortune; favored by fortune or luck; fortunate, lucky."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A happy event, thing, person, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/happy"},{"term":"margarine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spread, manufactured from a blend of vegetable oils (some of which are hydrogenated), emulsifiers etc, mostly used as a substitute for butter.","The solid ingredient of human fat, olive oil, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spread or cover (something) with margarine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/margarine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Margarine","blocks":[{"text":"Margarine is a spread used for flavoring, baking, and cooking. It is most often used as a substitute for butter. Although originally made from animal fats, most margarine consumed today is made from vegetable oil. The spread was originally named oleomargarine from Latin for oleum and Greek margarite. The name was later shortened to margarine, or sometimes oleo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Margarine.jpg/330px-Margarine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margarine","wikidata":"Q4287"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Margarine.jpg/500px-Margarine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Margarine.jpg/500px-Margarine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://e